This ascension occurred on July 19th, 2006, a little over a month after my
first ascension as Aaron the Wizard.  I've been a bit slow about posting
it.  Overall, I found the barbarian ascension to be relatively easy, and I 
think this was my second or third barbarian.  Of course, I also had the 
experience of my first ascension, which made a big difference.

I can think of only a few mistakes a made in the course of this game.  
Early on, I misidentified a scroll of destroy armor and read it, and it
destroyed my gauntlets of dexterity.  I didn't find another pair until I
made it to the Astral Plane, and at that point, there wasn't much point to
switching.

Because, as a chaotic character, I had Stormbringer, at one point, I 
accidentally struck the Minetown priest, who was co-aligned.  I tried 
casting charm monster, but that didn't help.  So, I did the following:  
wore a ring of teleport control, read a blessed scroll of detect monsters 
in order to see exactly where the priest was without a blindfold, 
teleported next to the priest, and read a blessed scroll of taming.  That 
did the trick, and after this point, I was extremely careful.

At the bottom of the mines, I stepped on a polymorph trap, and it turned 
me into a very weak elf.  I didn't have my pet around to protect me, so I 
waited it out in a corner, hoping that no monster would find me.  I guess 
that I was lucky, because no monsters turned up, and I eventually turned 
back into a human.

The only other point where I was in trouble was during the quest, when I 
was surrounded by trolls and giants.  I think I got out of that 
predicament by reading a scroll of teleportation.

At one point, I thought that I was in the process of being turned to stone
by a cockatrice, so I cast stone to flesh.  A little bit later, I
discovered that I was no longer carrying the Heart of Ahriman and couldn't
figure out how it had disappeared.  I thought that maybe a monster had
stolen it and spent some time searching for it.  Eventually, it dawned on
me that my spell had converted it into a meatball!  This artifact isn't 
all that useful, so it was just a minor inconvience not to have it.

Asmodeus was a real pain.  He had a wand of digging and kept on escaping
down a hole before I had a chance to kill him.  I ended up wearing a ring
of free action and using two potions of paralysis on him to get him to
stop moving for a long enough period of time to kill him.

By sacrificing, I also got Frost Brand, and I switched back and forth 
between Frost Brand and Stormbringer as needed (I mostly only used 
Stormbringer when faced with level-draining monsters).

The end game went pretty smoothly.  All the elemental planes were pretty 
easy.  On the Astral Plane, I first tried Famine, wrong altar, then tried 
Pestilence, and it was the right altar:

